SNAEXP V1.0 - READ.ME file
----------------------------

Welcome to my Expenses Manager Program V1.0.  

The archive should contain the following files:

\APP\SNAEXP0.APP               Main program

\APP\SNAEXP\SNACAR0.OVL        Optional Overlay File	
\APP\SNAEXP\SNAEXPH.OVL        Optional Help file
\APP\SNAEXP\SNAEXPP.OVL        Optional Print file

\OPD\SNAPRINT.DYL       Optional Print file

README.NEW         'Get you started' instructions for new users

HISTORY.TXT        Details of the various upgrades the program has gone through.

REGISTER.TXT       Details on how to register the program.
LICENCE.TXT        A legal document

SNAEXP0.DOC        Full instructions in Word format
SNAEXP0.TXT        Full instructions in ASCII Text format

I would strongly encourage you to read the instructions, but
if you still insist on flying blind:

To Install the program, do the following:

1.    Put SNAEXP0.APP into any \APP\ directory 

2.    If you have a Company Vehicle and would like to use the optional vehicle 
      monitor put the SNACAR0.OVL module into an \APP\SNAEXP\ directory.

3.    If you want to use the optional On-Line Help (Highly recommended) put the 
      file SNAEXPH.OVL into the \APP\SNAEXP\ directory.

4.    If you want to use the optional Print option put the file SNAEXPP.OVL into 
      the \APP\SNAEXP\ directory and the file SNAPRINT.DYL into an \OPD\ directory.  
      Note that this file is common to all my programs, so if you have more than one 
      of them you only need one copy of this file.

5.    Install as usual, using <PSION-I>.


If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions.  I have yet to 
be asked a question that wasn't already fully explained in the instructions !!

All comments, and registrations, still gratefully received.

If you wish to register, up-to-date details are in the file REGISTER.TXT

If you want to monitor progress on upgrades and enhancements, as well as see if 
any bugs have been reported, visit my home page on the World-Wide Web. The address is :  

http://ourworld.compuserve.com/homepages/alanrichey

